# Base URL of the 1Fi Marketplace API.
#
# Leave BLANK for local development:
#   - Web / iOS simulator  -> falls back to http://localhost:4000
#   - Physical Android/iOS device on the same Wi-Fi as Metro -> the app auto-uses
#     your machine's LAN IP on port 4000 (derived from the Expo host).
#
# Set this for a standalone / deployed build:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://onefi-marketplace-api.onrender.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=

# --- Google sign-in (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# Create OAuth client IDs at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# and paste them here. Any left blank just disable that platform; with all blank,
# the app falls back to the developer sign-in on the Profile tab.
#
#   Web client ID     — used by the web build AND the Expo Go / dev-client flow.
#                       Add your dev origin (e.g. http://localhost:8082) to both
#                       "Authorized JavaScript origins" and "Authorized redirect URIs".
#   Android client ID — needs the app package (in.onefi.marketplace) + signing SHA-1.
#   iOS client ID     — needs the bundle id (in.onefi.marketplace).
#
# The same Web client ID must also be listed in server/.env GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
